From: QEMU AT91 test suite <qemu-devel@nongnu.org>
Subject: [PATCH] lwip: enable the loopback interface for self-tests

The g45tcpself overlay command streams TCP over 127.0.0.1 to separate
stack behaviour from the MACB driver path when investigating the
streaming-TCP heap corruption.  The port's lwipopts pins
LWIP_HAVE_LOOPIF to 0 and leaves LWIP_NETIF_LOOPBACK at its default 0,
so self-addressed traffic is unroutable.  Enable both; profiles that do
not build lwip are unaffected.

---
 components/net/lwip/port/lwipopts.h | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/components/net/lwip/port/lwipopts.h b/components/net/lwip/port/lwipopts.h
--- a/components/net/lwip/port/lwipopts.h
+++ b/components/net/lwip/port/lwipopts.h
@@ -82,7 +82,8 @@
 #define LWIP_DNS                    0
 #endif

-#define LWIP_HAVE_LOOPIF            0
+#define LWIP_HAVE_LOOPIF            1
+#define LWIP_NETIF_LOOPBACK         1

 #define LWIP_PLATFORM_BYTESWAP      0

